WEBVTT

00:00:10.029 --> 00:00:11.730
Not that I've been getting any sleep lately,

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:13.830
but this had better be important.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.030
Your father's will dictated certain articles

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:18.230
be delivered to his surviving heir.

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:20.329
This particular line item wasn't discovered

00:00:20.329 --> 00:00:26.010
until after Lex passed.

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:27.510
You can imagine our surprise

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:30.510
when Lionel's heir turned out to be you.

00:00:30.510 --> 00:01:02.049
Clark.

00:01:02.049 --> 00:01:03.350
Calling another woman at this hour,

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:05.650
what would the industrious Lois Lane think?

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:06.849
We have a lead.

00:01:06.849 --> 00:01:12.739
Meet me at Cadmus Labs.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:38.709
I'll be right there.

00:01:38.709 --> 00:01:39.709
Clark.

00:01:39.709 --> 00:01:43.129
What'd you find?

00:01:43.129 --> 00:01:46.030
Emil finally finished working through the files we found after the fire.

00:01:47.129 --> 00:01:49.629
There's one body still unaccounted for, LX-1-5.

00:01:52.299 --> 00:01:53.500
There's another Lex on the loose.

00:01:54.799 --> 00:01:57.299
I look here. I closed the book on this place months ago.

00:01:57.299 --> 00:01:59.299
Supplies are still being sent here.

00:01:59.299 --> 00:02:09.389
Someone's helping him survive, but...

00:02:09.389 --> 00:02:12.389
You're assuming that he's a threat just because he's a Lutheran.

00:02:13.389 --> 00:02:15.889
Whatever happened to everyone deserving a second chance?

00:02:15.889 --> 00:02:20.650
Luther blood is Luther blood. It's poison.

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:21.650
It's here.

00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:22.650
Jeter room in the building.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:24.650
room in the building that's lead-lined.

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:28.599
Wait, I'll handle this.

00:02:28.599 --> 00:02:29.599
No, Tess.

00:02:29.599 --> 00:02:56.979
They're dangerous Tess, and they're born that way.

00:02:56.979 --> 00:03:00.979
I'll, I'll go back to Watchtower and see if I can program Oliver's satellite.

00:03:00.979 --> 00:03:05.979
Dearest Tess, thanks for the Reeb, but I'm all grown up now.

00:03:05.979 --> 00:03:17.590
Alexander, you knew about all this.

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:24.349
After everything Oliver and I did, to trust you, this is how you repay us?

00:03:24.349 --> 00:03:26.349
No. No, I was only trying to protect you.

00:03:26.349 --> 00:03:27.349
I was...

00:03:27.349 --> 00:03:28.349
Only trying to protect yourself.

00:03:28.349 --> 00:03:29.349
No.

00:03:29.349 --> 00:03:41.969
Clark.

00:03:41.969 --> 00:03:42.969
No better than he is.

00:03:42.969 --> 00:03:53.960
What else are you hiding, Tess?

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.960
It's a Cretonian relic.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:57.960
I only just received it.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.960
I swear to God I was going to tell you about it, Clark.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:00.960
It just showed up.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:01.960
Why do you have it?

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:10.500
Clark, there's something I need to tell you.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:47.490
Ah, now is the moment for an apocite quote from one of my favorites, Marcus Aurelius.

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:54.490
When you arise in the morning, think what a privilege it is to be alive, to breathe, to

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:57.290
joy to love, to think.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:57.990
Binal?

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.410
Dress yourself.

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:03.709
We Lutherman must seize our day.

00:05:03.709 --> 00:06:04.660
You only live once, son.

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:05.560
What are you doing here?

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:08.339
You shouldn't- I assume you will properly expense

00:06:08.339 --> 00:06:12.180
the services of the ladies Mandy and Bambi.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:15.399
We don't want to risk another audit.

00:06:15.399 --> 00:06:17.040
This is impossible.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:20.279
This ultraman persona you've come up with, genius.

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:22.259
It's a great way to strong arm our opponent.

00:06:22.279 --> 00:06:26.279
but your display of ego is attracting too much attention.

00:06:26.279 --> 00:06:27.279
You're getting reckless.

00:06:27.279 --> 00:06:28.279
Now button up.

00:06:28.279 --> 00:06:30.560
This a dream?

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:33.560
Absolutely. A dream that you were putting at risk.

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:35.560
Think, Clark.

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:38.560
Think what it took to build this empire.

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:41.560
Hard work. Dedication to family.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:48.730
And more than a little spilt blood.

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:49.730
It's...

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:51.730
It's one of my trials.

00:06:51.730 --> 00:06:55.730
No, no. Practice. You just need a little practice.

00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:56.730
You know what they say.

00:06:56.730 --> 00:07:00.730
say, burning the candle at both ends, trite but true.

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:07.350
I don't want to watch you making stupid mistakes, Clark.

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:11.350
I know what you're capable of. You can make a father proud.

00:07:11.350 --> 00:07:16.230
I'm not your son.

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:20.230
You watch out for those emotional reactions.

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:33.199
The heart. It'll blind you, son.

00:07:33.199 --> 00:07:37.199
You want to be your own man. That's natural.

00:07:37.199 --> 00:07:39.199
But remember, Clark.

00:07:39.199 --> 00:07:40.199
I am.

00:07:40.199 --> 00:07:47.199
your father and I alone raised you in my own image to become the man that you are today.

00:07:47.199 --> 00:07:52.819
I must have lost perspective.

00:07:52.819 --> 00:08:02.459
But that's why I'm here to set you back on the right path.

00:08:02.459 --> 00:08:07.110
The universe.

00:08:07.110 --> 00:08:10.110
The man of tomorrow, Clark Luther!

00:08:10.110 --> 00:08:19.689
I sometimes shudder to think what would have happened to my little traveler

00:08:19.689 --> 00:08:23.689
if he had been discovered in that cornfield by the first ignorant farmer that

00:08:23.689 --> 00:08:24.689
farmer that came along.

00:08:24.689 --> 00:08:29.189
Where on earth would you be now?

00:08:29.189 --> 00:08:49.490
Dad?

00:08:49.490 --> 00:09:00.259
He isn't here.

00:09:00.259 --> 00:09:07.600
How long have you been here?

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:09.600
Long enough to go for a ride.

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:11.600
You love to make me wait, don't you?

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:15.840
What are you doing?

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.840
Stop worrying.

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:19.840
Father will never find us here.

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:21.840
Father? Mm-hmm. Our father?

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:23.840
Last time I checked, you're still adopted,

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:26.840
and I'm still as red-headed bastard as it gets.

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:27.840
You're Luther.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:29.840
God, you love to rile me up, don't you?

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:30.840
Tess, I can't do this?

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:32.840
I can't do this.

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:34.840
Why not?

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:40.840
I'm not who you think I am.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:43.759
Your scar.

00:09:43.759 --> 00:09:44.759
Where's your scar?

00:09:44.759 --> 00:09:51.659
You bastard.

00:09:51.659 --> 00:09:54.659
He used the mirror box. He tells me all about it.

00:09:54.659 --> 00:09:56.659
And then he says he can't find it.

00:09:56.659 --> 00:09:58.659
I can't believe I ever thought it would work with us.

00:09:58.659 --> 00:10:00.659
I can't believe I ever trusted him.

00:10:00.659 --> 00:10:05.629
Tess, I found it.

00:10:05.629 --> 00:10:06.629
I used it.

00:10:06.629 --> 00:10:08.629
But who are you talking about?

00:10:08.629 --> 00:10:11.940
You.

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:17.730
Well, the more fun version of you, anyway.

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:18.730
Is this time travel?

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:20.730
Something went wrong in my past,

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:22.730
and if I fix it, I get to go back?

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:25.730
Are you really this naive in your world?

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:29.970
My world.

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:31.970
Tess, I need some help, all right?

00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:34.970
You obviously know something. You need to tell me.

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:36.970
Tess, please.

00:10:36.970 --> 00:10:43.100
According to my Clark, it's like a parallel reality.

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:45.100
It's still the same history.

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:48.100
It's just rewritten with a sort of darker edge.

00:10:48.100 --> 00:10:51.100
So while I'm stranded here, he's...

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:55.340
Stuck in your life there.

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:56.340
And you're kinder, gentle.

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:58.340
in our world is about to get an explosive awakening.

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:36.340
Well, in all the streets, in the whole world,

00:11:36.340 --> 00:11:38.340
you're the person I have to hit?

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:42.779
Boss, I'm so happy to see you.

00:11:42.779 --> 00:11:44.779
Hey, you know what, don't think for a minute

00:11:44.779 --> 00:11:46.779
that you're going to use this non-fender vendor

00:11:46.779 --> 00:11:48.779
as another excuse to try to get me fired.

00:11:48.779 --> 00:11:50.779
Lewis, why would I want to fire you?

00:11:50.779 --> 00:11:52.779
Because you're a masochist.

00:11:52.779 --> 00:11:56.980
No, I know why you're late. Are you okay?

00:11:56.980 --> 00:12:00.700
Mm-hmm.

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:04.700
Mr. Queen, any comment on the latest ground of land grabs in Smallville?

00:12:04.700 --> 00:12:06.700
Don't worry, Ali, I can handle this.

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:14.909
You're engaged?

00:12:14.909 --> 00:12:15.909
What your employees do with the person?

00:12:15.909 --> 00:12:17.909
in a life is none of your concern.

00:12:17.909 --> 00:12:20.909
Do you understand the people want to know what's going on?

00:12:20.909 --> 00:12:22.909
You're lucky to have her.

00:12:22.909 --> 00:12:24.909
How long have we'd known each other?

00:12:24.909 --> 00:12:27.909
Luther was boarding school, right?

00:12:27.909 --> 00:12:30.909
And how many times have I had to stand here

00:12:30.909 --> 00:12:32.909
and watch you piss away every single opportunity

00:12:32.909 --> 00:12:34.909
you've ever had to make this world a better place?

00:12:34.909 --> 00:13:15.730
Those don't belong to you.

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:19.929
Hey.

00:13:19.929 --> 00:13:20.929
Stay away from me.

00:13:20.929 --> 00:13:22.929
Why are you so afraid?

00:13:22.929 --> 00:13:29.740
Because no one sees Ultraman and lives to tell about it.

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:36.690
The line will turn me into a murderer.

00:13:36.690 --> 00:14:20.379
I turned me into a murderer.

00:14:20.379 --> 00:14:22.379
I thought I said I didn't want to be disturbed.

00:14:22.379 --> 00:14:26.379
It's adorable seeing you at my desk like you own the place.

00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:32.490
How can you be so flip when I've been looking for you all night long?

00:14:32.490 --> 00:15:00.789
It's so bothers you, doesn't it?

00:15:00.789 --> 00:15:03.789
There's no takebacks when it comes to Gold K.

00:15:03.789 --> 00:15:09.860
Lecture knew how to leave an impression, didn't he?

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:16.220
His ego certainly left something to be desired.

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:17.220
I am shocked.

00:15:17.220 --> 00:15:31.950
As disinterested as you were in finding the mirror box that you would bring us here.

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:32.950
Hardly any trace of vinyl at all.

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:33.950
Lionel at all?

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:40.330
It's refreshing, actually, being out from under our father's shadow.

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:48.100
Lionel Luther has been dead for years.

00:15:48.100 --> 00:15:50.100
Lex killed him.

00:15:50.100 --> 00:15:53.100
I guess Lex did something right in this place.

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:58.100
I gotta tell you, sis, this alternate earth, it's a blast.

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:01.100
Doesn't feel right, though.

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:12.419
Not having blood on my hands before lunch.

00:16:12.419 --> 00:16:16.700
Well, that's the great thing about us being on our own now.

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:17.700
It's that you can have lunch whenever you want.

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:18.700
whenever you want.

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:23.580
And what if I was hungry now?

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:30.379
I'm watched constantly.

00:16:30.379 --> 00:16:31.379
Here.

00:16:31.379 --> 00:16:37.659
Where's the box, Tess?

00:16:37.659 --> 00:16:38.659
Why?

00:16:38.659 --> 00:16:43.669
We destroy the box.

00:16:43.669 --> 00:16:48.299
We destroy any chance of being sent back there.

00:16:48.299 --> 00:16:51.710
And nothing can stop us.

00:16:51.710 --> 00:16:53.710
Well, why don't you wait at the mansion?

00:16:53.710 --> 00:17:02.690
And I'll grab the box.

00:17:02.690 --> 00:17:04.690
And we can celebrate.

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:39.069
We'll know what hit it.

00:17:39.069 --> 00:17:42.069
Oh, no, you are not gonna ruin this gal's afternoon off.

00:17:42.069 --> 00:17:46.759
Just a regular black coffee, please.

00:17:46.759 --> 00:17:49.900
please.

00:17:49.900 --> 00:17:50.900
Quit your day, job.

00:17:50.900 --> 00:18:08.240
And leave all this, efficient funds.

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:11.240
Like hell, I just got paid.

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:13.240
Try again.

00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:15.240
Hello? Who is this?

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:17.240
Fine. Then I will just...

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:18.240
Do you want to talk to me?

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:21.289
Seriously?

00:18:21.289 --> 00:18:22.289
Seriously.

00:18:22.289 --> 00:18:23.289
Leave all this, Lane?

00:18:23.289 --> 00:18:27.779
Who wants to know?

00:18:27.779 --> 00:18:29.779
Whoever's on the other side of myself.

00:18:29.779 --> 00:18:39.480
Hello? If I'm calling you, Lane, it's for a reason.

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:40.480
Tess?

00:18:40.480 --> 00:18:42.480
How are you doing this?

00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:43.480
Look to your lab.

00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:46.480
Your other left?

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:51.549
Watchtower is everywhere.

00:18:51.549 --> 00:19:00.140
Now get up here. We have a problem.

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:02.140
Nice to meet you, Lois.

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:07.829
Test Mercer, if your little stunt ruined my credit.

00:19:07.829 --> 00:19:09.829
All this for a primitive business signal.

00:19:09.829 --> 00:19:11.829
Subject, damn, unavailable.

00:19:11.829 --> 00:19:15.430
Okay, I'm not really sure what you're doing,

00:19:15.430 --> 00:19:18.430
but I'm perfectly willing to run around in front at technology,

00:19:18.430 --> 00:19:20.430
if it'll lend a hand.

00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:22.430
Considering that I can't successfully round up the troops,

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:25.430
I just assumed that Watchtower was the safest place in the city.

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:26.430
For who?

00:19:26.430 --> 00:19:27.430
For you? From who?

00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:28.430
From Clark.

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:29.430
Wait, my Clark?

00:19:29.430 --> 00:19:31.430
Not exactly.

00:19:31.430 --> 00:19:35.430
And it's only a matter of time before he realizes that I'm not his Tess.

00:19:35.430 --> 00:19:42.140
He found us.

00:19:42.140 --> 00:20:10.089
Get up, Tess.

00:20:10.089 --> 00:20:13.089
Clark, if this is some kind of Red K episode, we can work this off.

00:20:13.089 --> 00:20:21.009
We're alone.

00:20:21.009 --> 00:20:23.009
I wouldn't worry about Lane, sis.

00:20:23.009 --> 00:20:27.700
It's remarkable what you can hear when you stop to listen.

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:29.700
You can't stay here.

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:33.559
I can do whatever I want.

00:20:33.559 --> 00:20:36.559
I'm not going back to Lionel's world.

00:20:36.559 --> 00:20:37.559
This is exactly what you.

00:20:37.559 --> 00:20:57.210
what it is, Lionels. This world will be mine.

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:58.210
And if I don't?

00:20:58.210 --> 00:21:37.890
A prodigal daughter, you've returned.

00:21:37.890 --> 00:21:40.890
It's too much to drop in on dear old dad from time to time?

00:21:40.890 --> 00:21:43.890
When you've turned your back on both your father and your fortune?

00:21:43.890 --> 00:21:44.890
Yes, it is.

00:21:44.890 --> 00:21:48.890
If you saw my back, it's only because you kicked me out the door.

00:21:48.890 --> 00:21:58.109
Research?

00:21:58.109 --> 00:22:07.230
Does this have anything to do with that ill-conceived coup

00:22:07.230 --> 00:22:10.990
you have been planning?

00:22:10.990 --> 00:22:11.990
I'd have no idea...

00:22:11.990 --> 00:22:13.990
Don't lie, Tess.

00:22:13.990 --> 00:22:27.140
no good at it. You never were.

00:22:27.140 --> 00:22:31.140
A little Greek tragedy you've been trying to drag your brother into.

00:22:31.140 --> 00:22:35.140
Oh, yes. I know all about that.

00:22:35.140 --> 00:22:38.140
I love him. Like you never will.

00:22:38.140 --> 00:22:40.140
Of course you love him. It's no mystery.

00:22:40.140 --> 00:22:43.140
Clark is a god among men.

00:22:43.140 --> 00:22:47.140
Though how he could love you, a consummate disappointment is beyond me.

00:22:47.140 --> 00:22:52.859
You're nothing but trouble, Tess. You're corrupting him.

00:22:52.859 --> 00:22:55.859
You take a good long look in the mirror at the person who's responsible for you.

00:22:55.859 --> 00:22:57.859
who's responsible for corrupting Clark.

00:22:57.859 --> 00:22:59.859
I have worked too long and too hard to let you

00:22:59.859 --> 00:23:03.859
a little half-bred tramp with a magdalene complex ruin everything.

00:23:03.859 --> 00:23:13.130
You just made this a lot easier.

00:23:13.130 --> 00:23:23.099
Get in here.

00:23:23.099 --> 00:23:26.099
Why couldn't you ever love me the way that you love Clark?

00:23:26.099 --> 00:23:30.099
Simply put, sweetheart, you're just not special enough.

00:23:30.099 --> 00:23:39.049
Your love is enough to save you

00:23:39.049 --> 00:23:43.049
when he stabs you in the back, you son of a bitch.

00:23:43.049 --> 00:23:51.220
Jarrell?

00:23:51.220 --> 00:23:52.200
I know you and I have

00:23:52.220 --> 00:23:54.220
on the best of terms right now, but...

00:23:54.220 --> 00:23:57.220
I'd call that an understatement.

00:23:57.220 --> 00:24:06.880
Of course your progenitor would have every right to hold a grudge,

00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:10.880
considering the extreme measures you and I took to silence him.

00:24:10.880 --> 00:24:13.880
Lionel, what are you doing here?

00:24:13.880 --> 00:24:17.289
Surveying our progress.

00:24:17.289 --> 00:24:24.700
You remember Lear, son?

00:24:24.700 --> 00:24:26.700
Shakespeare, King Lear.

00:24:26.700 --> 00:24:29.700
Wanted to abdicate, retire.

00:24:29.700 --> 00:24:31.700
Lear had three children.

00:24:31.700 --> 00:24:33.700
He tells them he will divide his children.

00:24:33.700 --> 00:24:38.700
will divide his kingdom between them, giving the largest portion to the one who loves him most.

00:24:38.700 --> 00:24:41.700
Two of the children declare their lavish devotion.

00:24:41.700 --> 00:24:47.700
The youngest, his favorite, is blunt and plain spoken.

00:24:47.700 --> 00:24:49.700
